Okay, so I finally ascended an Arch. I've come close before (got 
outfought on Astral) and not quite so close several times.

Running notes:

Nothing-special Arch. Gonna do Sokoban before Mines, but there's a zoo 
on the Sokoban start level of the main dungeon, and I don't have great 
armor (found elven mithril but that's it) and I'm wielding the original 
pickaxe. Maybe let's do mines instead. Into mines, find ghost of a Ro on 
minetown level. BUC its stuff, on the edge of Stressed, back out to a 
stash in the main dungeon. Engrave-ID wands and find WoW. Wow indeed. 2 
bl ?charging, bl+2 SDSM, bl +2 CoMR. Int is 15, let's play this as a 
spellcaster sort; besides, maybe there's a dwarf with a mattock around.

Continue through main dungeon, Sokoban (amulet), and on.

Original pet lasts to DL 15, XL 11, when it's crushed by an owlbear. I 
thought Grrl could take it. Dammit.

Fall through hole into level with cleared-out throne room. Hrm. Find 
ghost of Ro in the next room, with a pile of stuff. I still don't have a 
BoH. But what's this? Bag, not a sack, over across the room? Rogue 
dropped it to fight the Olog-hai, apparently. BoH, uncursed. Load it up, 
still at the far edge of burdened. Back to the mines to complete the 
mines and get a full BUC. 

Minetown altar is crossaligned (N); mines end is potions. In minetown, 
get all stuff price IDed, hrm, have blessed 80-$ scroll and a ton of 
cursed stuff from the bones piles. Take off most armor, wield the 
completely rusty mattock, get all the cursed stuff in main inventory. 
And the scroll is RC. Good. Dip a bunch of ! water into the one ! HW I 
had, bless the BoH and the unicorn horn, load back up, down to finish 
the mines. Hrm. Orcs, several orcs. I have all 4 300-$ rings uncursed 
and un-IDed. Find conflict. Same DL, find a poly trap. Remove cloak, put 
on another 300$ ring. Find =PC and spend a few turns as a Lich. Switch 
out rings to the third of the four and go to kill and eat a leprechaun. 
Oops, this ring is Poly, not a problem really but I don't want to be a 
silver dragon. Let a lynx kill me, back to dwarfhood with all four 300-$ 
rings IDed. Nice.

Mines end, find magic trap with open space on only two sides. Hang out 
there, lose a few HP from max and get speed boots burned, but ID =FA 
(gelatinous cube) and =Regenregeneration. inally get cold resistance 
from a winter wolf, after force bolting several blue jellies and getting 
nothing. Clear out without finishing the trap when a some lich thing 
shows up. 

First altars in main dungeon are unattended on DL21 (converted from N), 
then attended, also N, on 22. 8 pts of protection and counting. 28K 
turns. Five sacrifices (luck is already maxed out from a few gems to a 
white unicorn) and GS. Oookay.

Full ID, finally. What I had as Free Action is Searching. Damn. Have the 
rest of the major rings (Regen, Conflict [which I don't use but don't 
mind having], SD, Levitation, TC). Really shouldn't have gone for 
teleportitis, even with the =TC. I find it more of a hassle than a 
bonus. Ah, well, next time. Un ID-ed amulet is MB, cool. Still haven't 
seen ?Geno (and there's a MF waiting for me at the portal to the quest, 
so that needs to happen). Enchant up SDSM, CoMR, speed boots, GS. AC -
24, GS +6. 

So now there are altars on nearly every level? [21-22, 24, 25, plus one 
or two more before the Castle, IIRC]

Barracks on DL 25. Captain has /Death. I have reflection and MR and now 
a /Death. I'm ready for Medusa and the Castle depending on how many Ls 
are there. I suppose I could recharge that /Wish and get some scrolls, 
but that seems too easy. But I haven't seen the scroll so I'm not going 
to try to write it.

Medusa is middle island. Do the Castle through the back, set up another 
cache in VoD. ID more spellbooks, including ID. Kewl. Several full IDs, 
finish VoD, time for the quest.

Quest is totally easy, find +Map at quest leader's chest. Kewl. [Mapping 
is the A's special spell.]

Hrm. Still missing ?Punish and ?Geno. Had one 300$ scroll IDed, but 
don't see it anywhere-- maybe it got blanked in moat carelessness? Doing 
okay in melee against Ls and MFs, but I don't want to go to endgame with 
them still around. Suppose I have all of hell to worry about that. Also 
have /s-wish at 1:2 (used one more for a marker) and 0:1, so I could get 
the scroll if I really need it.

Wow-- I wasn't fire resistant. Finally found a flesh golem on 
Baalzebub's to take care of that. 

Geno Ls after a MasterLich starts summoning, including a MMF. So much 
for no genocide. +MM the MMF, though. +MM is really working well; I'm 
pleased.

Lalala. Finally ready, unburdened, lots of alchemy, 363 HP, -39 AC, turn 
63K.

Met Yeenoghu in Rodney's tower.

Down to VS, why won't this thing work? Okay, so you have to be on the 
vibrating square, not next to it. I know this. Recharge the Bell, 4 
?charging left.

Slog through Moloch's, cursed!GL to get out. (Whoever thought of this, 
thanks. First time I remembered to do it.)

Going back up: Met Rodney a total of 5 times: his tower, DL47(VS), DL45, 
DL30 (Vod), Earth.

Had Force issues:  Force: 43-45, 45-46, 44-45, 43-46, 41-41, 41-43, 42-
44, 44-46,45-46,35-36,35-35,35-3,36-37,31-33, Met a Disenchanter 
somewhere along the way that took my GS down to +6. Also found a magic 
marker sitting around.

On to planes. One !FH on Air at about 110 HP. Reach Water at turn 66924, 
Astral at ~67K. Arrive toward the left, spend what seems like too many 
turns getting configured (change =Lev for SD, eat, get magic whistle and 
magic lamp out, deal with Burdened and no space in pack issues).

Death is left, Famine, center, Pestilence right. I've lost an A on 
Astral before--somehow even with GS they don't fight that well. I know 
Death is a wimp, but I want to keep my max HP up. So, to the middle and 
Famine and leave the Angel to do what it wants, Quaff another !FH in the 
melee.

Middle altar is Lawful. Magic whistle the angel, offer.

So, I've ascended W, V (3.3.1), B, S, P, C, A (3.4). Ro or K next, I 
think.

-S

